  "term": "psychophysical properties",
  "definition": "Psychophysical properties are the measurable features of a person’s sensory experience in relation to physical stimulation. In this source, the term refers to how the tingling sensation changes over time, with repeated exposure, and with factors such as temperature and touch sensitivity.",
